======================================================================
POST-HOC NOTE
======================================================================
The r_5bp / r_15bp / r_total values printed in the section above were
calculated with a buggy formula (r = 1 - 2U/(n1*n2)), which gives the
WRONG sign: when pathogenic > benign, r came out negative.

The CORRECT rank-biserial correlation (Kerby 2014) is
r = 2U/(n1*n2) - 1, where U is scipy's U1 statistic (high U means
group 1 stochastically greater under alternative='greater').

The corrected r values are saved in summary_by_gene.csv and
meta_analysis.csv. With the correction, r values are POSITIVE when
pathogenic > benign:

  DMD:       r_5bp = +0.695, p = 7.99e-07
  CFTR:      r_5bp = +0.088, p = 0.318 (ns)
  SCN1A:     r_5bp = +0.421, p = 0.0070
  Combined:  r_5bp = +0.467, p = 7.99e-07
  Fisher meta across 3 genes: p = 3.16e-06

The ISM data itself (metrics.csv, metrics_per_alt.csv, npy files) is
unchanged; only the effect-size formula and resulting summary CSVs
were updated. The ism_dnase_n30.py script has been patched with the
correct formula and will reproduce these values on any rerun.
